sentences.text:
The petitioner is directed to be enlarged on bail in Crime No.69/2025 of Tumakuru Town Police Station registered for the offences punishable under Sections 4, 5 and 6 of the Prize Chits & Money Circulation Schemes (Banning) Act, 1978, Section 9 of the Karnataka Protection of Interest Depositors in Financial Establishment Act 2004 and Sections 120B, 406, 409, 420 and 114 read with Section 34 of IPC, subject to the following conditions:
NC: 2025:KHC:19201 HC-KAR T Shivanandamurthy vs The State Of Karnataka on 6 June, 2025 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/61933306/
3 a) Petitioner shall execute personal bond for a sum of Rs.1,00,000/- with two sureties for the likesum, to the satisfaction of the jurisdictional Court;
b) The petitioner shall appear regularly on all the dates of hearing before the Trial Court unless the Trial Court exempts his appearance for valid reasons;
c) The petitioner shall not directly or indirectly threaten or tamper with the prosecution witnesses;
d) The petitioner shall not involve in similar offences in future;
e) The petitioner shall not leave the jurisdiction of the Trial Court without permission of the said Court until the case registered against him is disposed off.
SD/-
(S VISHWAJITH SHETTY) JUDGE PGG T Shivanandamurthy vs The State Of Karnataka on 6 June, 2025 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/61933306/
